cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sparse Index Tracker"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gupta
    given-names: Pratyush
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/PratyushGupta7/Sparse-Index-Tracker"
url: "https://sparse-index-tracker.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Sparse index replication engine that tracks major equity indices
  (S&P 500, Nasdaq-100, Russell 2000, Nifty 50) with roughly 10% of
  each index's constituents using a custom ADMM solver for
  L1-regularized, long-only portfolio optimization. Includes
  walk-forward backtests, eight-regime stress tests, a FastAPI
  backend, a Next.js frontend, and a full cloud deployment.
keywords:
  - sparse index tracking
  - index replication
  - portfolio optimization
  - ADMM
  - L1 regularization
  - convex optimization
  - direct indexing
  - tax-loss harvesting
  - quantitative finance
  - LASSO
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-20"
